cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SplatThis: portable 2D Gaussian splat artifacts"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alkema
    given-names: Bram
repository-code: "https://github.com/BramAlkema/SplatThis"
license: MIT
version: 0.3.1
date-released: "2026-08-07"
keywords:
  - gaussian-splatting
  - svg
  - powerpoint
  - canvas
  - css
  - mlx
  - steganography
  - image-vectorization
abstract: >-
  SplatThis fits anisotropic 2D Gaussian splats to a bitmap with Torch and
  exports the fitted population as SVG, native PowerPoint, Canvas HTML, CSS
  HTML, or CSS-based EML, with optional MLX fitting, browser capture, and
  recoverable population carriers.
